# Frontend Development Rules

## Tech Stack

- **React 19** with functional components and hooks
- **React Router 7** (file-based routing in `app/routes/`)
- **Tailwind CSS 4** with CSS variables for theming
- **TanStack Query** for server state management
- **Radix UI** for accessible primitives
- **Motion** (Framer Motion) for animations
- **React Three Fiber** for 3D visualizations

## Project Structure

```
apps/front/app/
├── api/           # API client functions (fetch wrappers)
├── components/    # React components organized by feature
│   ├── ui/        # Reusable UI primitives (shadcn/ui style)
│   └── [feature]/ # Feature-specific components
├── context/       # React contexts
├── hooks/         # Custom React hooks
├── lib/           # Utilities (http client, utils)
├── providers/     # Provider components
├── routes/        # React Router route components
└── types/         # TypeScript type definitions
```

## Component Guidelines

### Component Structure
```tsx
import { useState, useCallback, useMemo } from 'react';
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

interface MyComponentProps {
  title: string;
  onAction?: () => void;
}

export function MyComponent({ title, onAction }: MyComponentProps) {
  // Hooks first
  const [state, setState] = useState(false);
  
  // Derived values with useMemo
  const computed = useMemo(() => /* ... */, [deps]);
  
  // Callbacks with useCallback
  const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
    onAction?.();
  }, [onAction]);
  
  // Render
  return (
    <div className="...">
      {title}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### UI Components

UI primitives live in `components/ui/` and follow shadcn/ui patterns:
- Use `class-variance-authority` (cva) for variants
- Use `cn()` utility for class merging
- Support `asChild` pattern via Radix Slot when needed
- Include proper TypeScript props with `ComponentProps`

Example pattern:
```tsx
const variants = cva("base-classes", {
  variants: {
    variant: {
      default: "default-classes",
      secondary: "secondary-classes",
    },
    size: {
      default: "size-default",
      sm: "size-sm",
      lg: "size-lg",
    },
  },
  defaultVariants: {
    variant: "default",
    size: "default",
  },
});
```

## TanStack Query Usage

### Query Pattern
```tsx
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { fetchRoverImages } from '@/api/rover';

export function useRoverImages(params: RoverParams) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['rover-images', params],
    queryFn: () => fetchRoverImages(params),
    staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // 5 minutes
  });
}
```

### API Client Pattern
```tsx
// api/rover.ts
import { httpClient } from '@/lib/http';

export async function fetchRoverImages(params: RoverParams) {
  const response = await httpClient.get('/api/v1/rover-image', { params });
  return response.data;
}
```

## Styling with Tailwind

### Design Tokens
- Use CSS variables for colors: `bg-primary`, `text-foreground`
- Dark mode support via `.dark` class
- Responsive design: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:` breakpoints

### Common Patterns
```tsx
// Conditional classes with cn()
<div className={cn(
  "base-classes",
  isActive && "active-classes",
  className
)} />

// Space-themed dark backgrounds
<div className="bg-[#02030a]" /> // Deep space black
<div className="bg-slate-900/95" /> // Semi-transparent dark
```

### Animation
- Use `motion` library for complex animations
- CSS transitions for simple hover effects
- GSAP available for advanced timeline animations

## Form Handling

Use TanStack Form for complex forms:
```tsx
import { useForm } from '@tanstack/react-form';

const form = useForm({
  defaultValues: { /* ... */ },
  onSubmit: async ({ value }) => { /* ... */ },
});
```

## Performance

- Use `useMemo` for expensive computations
- Use `useCallback` for callbacks passed to children
- Lazy load heavy components with `React.lazy()`
- Use `Suspense` boundaries for loading states
- Implement proper loading skeletons

## Error Handling

- Use error boundaries for component errors
- Show toast notifications for API errors with `react-hot-toast`
- Provide fallback UI for failed data fetching

## Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include proper ARIA attributes via Radix primitives
- Support keyboard navigation
- Maintain good color contrast ratios
